  "api": "discoveryengine.v1beta",
  "service": "Vertex AI Agent Builder",
  "title": "Breaking Changes: Read-Only Fields; New Feature Toggles & OAuth Scopes",
  "summary": "This update introduces breaking changes by making several fields read-only across Engine, Project, and AssistAnswer schemas. Developers must update any code attempting to write to these properties. Additionally, new capabilities include customer-managed OAuth scopes for connectors, global feature toggle controls for engines, and the ability to specify provisioning intent for projects.",
  "details": "Several properties have been made read-only/immutable, which is a breaking change. Specifically, `delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed` and `effectiveFeatures` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine` (and its alpha/beta counterparts), `experienceState` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Project` (and alpha/beta), and `toolDisplayNames` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistAnswer` (and beta) can no longer be modified. If your applications attempt to write to these fields, they will now encounter errors.\n\nOn the new features front, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ActionConfig` (and `v1alpha`) now supports `customerManagedScopes`, allowing you to specify custom OAuth scopes for connectors that opt into this feature, providing more granular control over permissions. Engines gain new feature management capabilities with the `globalFeatureToggleState` property, enabling control over feature rollout strategies (e.g., `DELAYED`, `SCHEDULED`, `GENERAL`, `EARLY`), and the `effectiveFeatures` output-only map to see the resolved state of all feature toggles. When provisioning a project, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaProvisionProjectRequest` now includes a `provisionIntent` field, letting you specify the desired experience (`SOBI_ONLY`, `LEGACY_ONLY`). Finally, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DynamicTool` (and `v1alpha`) introduces a `readonly` boolean property to indicate if a tool performs write operations, and `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistAnswer` (and `v1beta`) now exposes `toolDisplayNames` for human-readable tool titles.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
